---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "Weslo Treadmills (2026): What Happened to the Brand, and What to Buy Instead";
const description =
  "Weslo was iFIT’s cheapest treadmill brand, sold mainly through Walmart. What is left of the range, parts for owners, and Amazon treadmills in the same price tier.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: "nordictrack-t-series-5-weslo-alt",
    name: "NordicTrack T Series 5",
    brand: "NordicTrack",
    category: "Alternative on Amazon: iFIT’s current entry treadmill",
    badge: "Closest Successor",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CJ9W38VQ?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31HBQOJxIZL._SL500_.jpg","width":386,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $469 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":469,"high":469},
    specs: "0–10 mph · 0–10% incline · KeyFlex cushioning · LCD display · iFIT Train membership for auto workouts · about 130 lb",
    pros: [
      "Made by iFIT, the same company that made Weslo",
      "Powered incline to 10%, against a Weslo’s two manual positions",
      "Works with iFIT classes from your own phone or tablet",
      "Syncs with Strava, Garmin and Apple with a membership, per the listing",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Many headline features need a paid iFIT Train membership",
      "Belt size and motor rating not given in the bullet points we read",
      "More than a Weslo used to cost",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The nearest thing to a new Weslo: iFIT’s cheapest treadmill, with powered incline and optional classes.",
    description: "Weslo no longer has a new treadmill on Amazon, so this card is an alternative. The T Series 5 is the entry point to NordicTrack’s range and, in practice, the treadmill that now fills Weslo’s old role inside iFIT. The listing gives speeds up to 10 mph, a 0 to 10% incline, KeyFlex cushioning and an LCD display, and says you can use your own phone or tablet to follow iFIT trainers who adjust the treadmill automatically. Those automatic workouts, the ActivePulse heart-rate control, SmartAdjust, Google Maps routes and app syncing all need an iFIT Train membership, according to the listing; without one, it is a straightforward motorised treadmill. Amazon gives the item weight as 130 lb. It was $469.27 on 9 November 2026. The bullet points we read did not state a belt size, motor rating, user weight limit or warranty term, so check NordicTrack’s own specification page before ordering. Our T Series guide covers the rest of the range.",
  },
  {
    id: "xterra-trx1000-weslo-alt",
    name: "Xterra Fitness TRX1000 Compact Series Treadmill",
    brand: "XTERRA",
    category: "Alternative on Amazon: closest in format to the Cadence G 5.9",
    badge: "Closest in Format",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FBKNYX52?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/418VaHJC4zL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $446 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":446,"high":446},
    specs: "2.25 HP motor · 16 x 50 in. belt · 5 in. LCD · folding deck · steel frame · about 104 lb",
    pros: [
      "The same 2.25 HP rating and 16 by 50-inch belt as the Cadence G 5.9",
      "A simple console with no subscription built in",
      "Folding deck and a heavy-duty steel frame, per the listing",
      "XTERRA is an established budget treadmill maker",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Amazon listing does not state the incline, speed or capacity",
      "Basic five-inch LCD",
      "Manual incline only, by XTERRA’s own figures used in our Weslo review",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a buyer who wants a new machine that works like the old Weslo: simple, folding and subscription-free.",
    description: "This card is an alternative, not a Weslo. If what you liked about the Cadence G 5.9 was its simplicity, the TRX1000 is the closest match we found on Amazon. The listing gives a quiet 2.25 HP motor, a 16 by 50-inch walking and running surface, a five-inch LCD, a heavy-duty steel frame and console crossbar, and a folding deck, and Amazon puts the weight at about 104 lb. Those are almost exactly the Weslo’s motor rating and belt size. The Amazon listing is brief and does not give the incline, top speed, user weight limit or warranty; XTERRA’s own figures, as checked for our Cadence G 5.9 review, give three manual incline levels, a 10 mph top speed and a 250 lb rating, slightly below the Weslo’s 275 lb, with a lifetime frame warranty. Confirm those on XTERRA’s site before you buy. It was $445.99 on 9 November 2026. Like the Weslo, it suits walking and light jogging a few times a week.",
  },
  {
    id: "goplus-375hp-weslo-alt",
    name: "Goplus 3.75HP Folding Treadmill with Incline",
    brand: "Goplus",
    category: "Alternative on Amazon: powered incline for less",
    badge: "Most Incline for the Money",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09D814HYX?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41CduzRJ71L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $430 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":430,"high":430},
    specs: "1–15% automatic incline · 52 x 17 in. belt · 3.75 HP · 265 lb capacity · 12 preset + 3 custom programs · soft-drop folding",
    pros: [
      "Automatic incline to 15%, far beyond a Weslo’s two positions",
      "A 52-inch belt, two inches longer than the Cadence G 5.9’s",
      "Soft-drop folding and four transport wheels",
      "Handrail heart-rate sensors, Bluetooth speakers and app control",
    ],
    cons: [
      "265 lb capacity, below the Weslo’s 275 lb",
      "Top speed not given in the bullet points we read",
      "Goplus is a marketplace brand with less established support than iFIT",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a Weslo owner who wants to swap manual incline for a powered 15% range without spending more.",
    description: "This card is an alternative, not a Weslo. Goplus’s 3.75 HP folding treadmill sits in the same price band a Weslo used to, and offers a good deal more incline. The listing gives an automatic incline of 1 to 15%, 12 preset and three user-defined programs, a 52 by 17-inch five-layer belt, a 3.75 HP motor, a 265 lb maximum load, a five-inch LCD, four Bluetooth speakers, app control and handrail heart-rate sensors. It folds vertically with a soft-drop system and rolls on four wheels. Amazon puts the weight at 140 lb. It was $429.99 on 9 November 2026. Two things to weigh. The 265 lb limit is lower than the Cadence G 5.9’s published 275 lb, so heavier users should leave a margin. And Goplus is a large marketplace seller rather than a specialist treadmill maker, so check the warranty and returns on the listing you buy from. The bullet points we read did not state a top speed.",
  },
  {
    id: "therun-12-weslo-alt",
    name: "THERUN Incline Treadmill, 0-12% Auto Incline",
    brand: "THERUN",
    category: "Alternative on Amazon: cheapest powered incline",
    badge: "Cheapest Alternative",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DJ8F6DZP?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41TP5tk6XaL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $340 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":340,"high":340},
    specs: "0–12% auto incline, 12 levels · 43.3 x 16.5 in. belt · 0.5–9 mph · 3.0 HP · 300 lb capacity · folding",
    pros: [
      "Powered incline to 12% for about $340",
      "300 lb rating, above the Weslo’s 275 lb",
      "Folds and stores, with straightforward assembly per the listing",
      "Four internal shock absorbers plus two cushioning layers",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 43.3-inch belt is shorter than a Weslo’s 50 inches",
      "Top speed 9 mph",
      "No warranty term in the bullet points we read",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest new folding treadmill with powered incline in this tier; best for walkers, given the shorter belt.",
    description: "This card is an alternative, not a Weslo. THERUN’s 12% auto-incline treadmill is the cheapest machine on this page and still offers something a Weslo never did: incline you change with a button. The listing gives 12 levels of automatic incline from 0 to 12%, a 3.0 HP motor, speeds of 0.5 to 9 mph, a 300 lb user rating and a 43.3 by 16.5-inch belt, with four internal shock absorbers and two extra layers of non-slip cushioning. It folds for storage and the listing describes assembly as straightforward. Amazon puts the weight at 110 lb. It was $339.99 on 9 November 2026. The trade-off is belt length. At 43.3 inches it is nearly seven inches shorter than the Cadence G 5.9’s belt, which is fine for walking but cramped for jogging, particularly for taller users. The listing refers to the machine as a walking pad in places, which is a fair hint at how to use it.",
  },
  {
    id: "proform-carbon-tl-weslo-alt",
    name: "ProForm Carbon TL",
    brand: "ProForm",
    category: "Alternative on Amazon: iFIT step-up",
    badge: "Best Step-Up",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BS4CRS8C?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31yv4f1FxpL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":488},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $598 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":598,"high":598},
    specs: "0–10 mph · 0–10% incline · ProShox cushioning · 5 in. LCD and device shelf · folds with hydraulic foot bar · about 166 lb",
    pros: [
      "An iFIT-built folding treadmill, like the Weslo was",
      "Powered incline to 10% and ProShox cushioning",
      "Hydraulic assist when lowering the deck",
      "Works with iFIT classes on your own device",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Many features need an iFIT Train membership",
      "Belt size, motor and capacity not in the bullet points we read",
      "The dearest alternative here",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a former Weslo owner who wants to stay with an iFIT machine and spend a little more on a sturdier folding frame.",
    description: "This card is an alternative, not a Weslo. ProForm is the iFIT brand that sat just above Weslo, and the Carbon TL is its cheapest treadmill on Amazon. The listing gives speeds up to 10 mph, a 0 to 10% incline, ProShox cushioning, a five-inch LCD with a device shelf, and a folding frame with a hydraulic foot bar that lowers the deck smoothly. As with the NordicTrack T Series 5, automatic trainer-led workouts, heart-rate control with ActivePulse, SmartAdjust and app syncing need an iFIT Train membership, according to the listing. Amazon gives the weight as about 166 lb, heavier than the T Series 5, which usually signals a more substantial frame. It was $598.00 on 9 November 2026. The bullet points did not state a belt size, motor rating, user weight limit or warranty, so check ProForm’s specification page. Our ProForm guide covers the rest of the range.",
  },
  {
    id: "shejio-weslo-g59-belt",
    name: "SHEJIO Treadmill Walking Belt Compatible with Weslo Cadence G 5.9 (WLTL296090)",
    brand: "SHEJIO",
    category: "For owners: replacement belt for the Cadence G 5.9",
    badge: "For Weslo Owners",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CFZYRFB9?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41V4LO+EnWL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":433},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $97 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":97,"high":97},
    specs: "Fits Weslo Cadence G 5.9 models WLTL296090, WLTL296130, WLTL296132 · two-layer PVC · anti-static wires · pre-lubricated · 1-year warranty",
    pros: [
      "Lists the exact WLTL model numbers it fits",
      "Pre-lubricated, with extra lubricant supplied",
      "Anti-static conductive wires in the belt",
      "One-year warranty from the seller",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Not for the G 5.9i, which has its own model numbers and its own belt listing",
      "A belt will not fix a failing motor or control board",
      "Third-party part, not from iFIT",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For an owner whose Cadence G 5.9 still runs but whose belt is worn, slipping or frayed.",
    description: "Most Weslo searches come from owners, and a worn belt is the commonest fault on a treadmill that has seen years of walking. This replacement from SHEJIO lists the three Cadence G 5.9 model numbers it fits, WLTL296090, WLTL296130 and WLTL296132; the same seller sells separate belts for the G 5.9i, G-40, LX45 and LS10/LX15, each with its own model numbers, so match the WLTL number on your frame sticker rather than the name. The listing describes a two-layer commercial-quality PVC belt with anti-static conductive wires, pre-lubricated, with a little extra lubricant supplied and a warning not to over-apply it, and recommends lubricating at least once a year. The seller offers a one-year warranty while the treadmill works normally. It was $96.99 on 9 November 2026. Before buying, check the belt is the cause: a slipping belt can also mean low tension or a dry deck, and hesitation under load can mean the motor or controller. Our replacement belts guide explains how to tell.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Weslo Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/weslo-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Weslo still make treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "We could not confirm any new Weslo treadmill on sale on 9 November 2026. Amazon US listed only Weslo replacement parts, independent reviewers describe recent Cadence models as discontinued, and we could not find a current new Weslo treadmill at Walmart, the brand’s main retailer. Used machines and parts are easy to find.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who makes Weslo treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Weslo was a brand of ICON Health & Fitness, which now trades as iFIT and also owns NordicTrack and ProForm. Weslo was the family’s entry-level line, sold mainly through mass retailers such as Walmart.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are Weslo treadmills sold on Amazon?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not new, on the day we checked. A search on 9 November 2026 returned replacement belts, safety keys and motors for Weslo models, but no Weslo treadmill. The closest new machine on Amazon from the same company is the NordicTrack T Series 5.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What can replace a Weslo Cadence treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "In the same price tier on Amazon, the NordicTrack T Series 5 (about $469) and ProForm Carbon TL (about $598) are iFIT’s current entry models, the XTERRA TRX1000 (about $446) is closest in format, and Goplus and THERUN sell folding treadmills with powered incline for $340 to $430.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Where do I find the model number on a Weslo treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On a sticker on the frame, usually near the front of the base or under the motor hood. Weslo model numbers start with WLTL, and replacement belts and keys are listed by that number rather than by the model name.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it worth fixing an old Weslo?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually, if the fault is a wear part: a belt, a safety key or lubrication costs far less than a new treadmill. If the motor or control board has failed, the repair can approach the price of a new budget machine, and parts for discontinued models get harder to find.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-09",
      dateModified: "2026-11-09",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 6,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/weslo-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/weslo-treadmills/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "brands");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-09",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-09",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "weslo treadmill",
      "weslo treadmills",
      "weslo cadence",
      "weslo cadence g 5.9i",
      "weslo cadence r 5.2",
      "weslo treadmill walmart",
      "weslo treadmill parts",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Closest Successor: NordicTrack T Series 5", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Brand Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Weslo Treadmills: Where the Brand Stands Now</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Weslo was the entry-level treadmill brand of ICON Health & Fitness, now iFIT, and for years its Cadence models were among the cheapest motorised treadmills in American big-box stores. Today they are hard to find new. Here is what we could confirm about the range, how to keep an old Weslo running, and what to buy in the same price tier on Amazon.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 9, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-5-weslo-alt"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31HBQOJxIZL._SL500_.jpg" alt="NordicTrack T Series 5" width="386" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#xterra-trx1000-weslo-alt"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/418VaHJC4zL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Xterra Fitness TRX1000 Compact Series Treadmill" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#goplus-375hp-weslo-alt"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41CduzRJ71L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Goplus 3.75HP Folding Treadmill with Incline" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>NordicTrack T Series 5 · Xterra Fitness TRX1000 Compact Series Treadmill · Goplus 3.75HP Folding Treadmill with Incline</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          People still search for Weslo treadmills in large numbers, mostly for one of two reasons.
          Some own one, often a Cadence bought at Walmart years ago, and want a belt, a safety key or
          a sense of whether it is worth fixing. Others remember Weslo as the cheap, reliable-enough
          name from the store aisle and want to buy another. This guide is for both. It explains who
          made Weslo machines and where they were sold, what we could and could not confirm about
          new Weslo treadmills on 9 November 2026, which parts for the best-known model are on
          Amazon, and which treadmills on Amazon today fill the same role: a folding motorised
          machine with some incline for walking and light jogging, for roughly $300 to $600.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest Successor:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-5-weslo-alt">NordicTrack T Series 5</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest in Format:</span> <a href="#xterra-trx1000-weslo-alt">Xterra Fitness TRX1000 Compact Series Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Incline for the Money:</span> <a href="#goplus-375hp-weslo-alt">Goplus 3.75HP Folding Treadmill with Incline</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Cheapest Alternative:</span> <a href="#therun-12-weslo-alt">THERUN Incline Treadmill, 0-12% Auto Incline</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Step-Up:</span> <a href="#proform-carbon-tl-weslo-alt">ProForm Carbon TL</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">For Weslo Owners:</span> <a href="#shejio-weslo-g59-belt">SHEJIO Treadmill Walking Belt Compatible with Weslo Cadence G 5.9 (WLTL296090)</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[5].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the products below.</strong> We have not tested these
          treadmills or parts. On 9 November 2026 we searched Amazon US for Weslo treadmills and found
          only replacement parts, so the treadmill cards on this page are alternatives in the same
          price tier, labelled as such. For each product we looked up the Amazon listing that day and
          recorded the price shown and what the listing says about motor, speed, incline, belt size,
          capacity and warranty. Every figure on a card comes from that listing; where a listing does
          not give a figure, we say so. We could not confirm that Walmart or anyone else currently
          sells new Weslo treadmills, so check any listing you find carefully. Prices change often. We
          earn a commission if you buy through the Amazon links on this page; it does not change which
          products we list or what we say about them.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">Can You Still Buy a Weslo Treadmill? The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-made-weslo">Who Made Weslo, and Where It Was Sold</a></li>
