        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does Weslo still make treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We could not confirm any new Weslo treadmill on sale on 9 November 2026. Amazon US listed only Weslo replacement parts, independent reviewers describe recent Cadence models as discontinued, and we could not find a current new Weslo treadmill at Walmart, the brand’s main retailer. Used machines and parts are easy to find.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes Weslo treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Weslo was a brand of ICON Health & Fitness, which now trades as iFIT and also owns NordicTrack and ProForm. Weslo was the family’s entry-level line, sold mainly through mass retailers such as Walmart.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are Weslo treadmills sold on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not new, on the day we checked. A search on 9 November 2026 returned replacement belts, safety keys and motors for Weslo models, but no Weslo treadmill. The closest new machine on Amazon from the same company is the NordicTrack T Series 5.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What can replace a Weslo Cadence treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              In the same price tier on Amazon, the NordicTrack T Series 5 (about $469) and ProForm Carbon TL (about $598) are iFIT’s current entry models, the XTERRA TRX1000 (about $446) is closest in format, and Goplus and THERUN sell folding treadmills with powered incline for $340 to $430.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where do I find the model number on a Weslo treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On a sticker on the frame, usually near the front of the base or under the motor hood. Weslo model numbers start with WLTL, and replacement belts and keys are listed by that number rather than by the model name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is it worth fixing an old Weslo?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually, if the fault is a wear part: a belt, a safety key or lubrication costs far less than a new treadmill. If the motor or control board has failed, the repair can approach the price of a new budget machine, and parts for discontinued models get harder to find.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

